{
  "_comment": "Large dragon wings (B5, the Ender Dragon's; the full library's dragon wings, G8 may reuse them): each wing a jointed frame in one plane parallel to the back, `depth` px behind it (default 6, so the folded wings lie over long hair rather than under it; a wearer with short hair may bring them in to 1.75), a short leather root on the rig's wing_r bridging the gap: an arm (humerus and forearm, wing_arm_r on the rig's wing_r) from the shoulder blade to the wrist, a knuckle with a pale claw (trim) at the wrist, three black finger bones (main) on wing_hand_r, wing_f2_r and wing_f3_r, and between them the membrane (alt: purple) as half-webs, each a triangle from the wrist (cutout tri_up) lying next to its finger, so the fan closes into a narrow fold and opens without a gap; thin veins in the detail colour (stripes with a gap) glow in the phase look (from phase 2). At rest the wings are FOLDED: the arm up and out so the wrist and its claw stand above the shoulder, the fingers and webs hanging down behind and beside the arm to the waist; any clip that does not key the part's bones shows them folded. A clip opens them by turning those bones about z (right wing: arm -50, hand +133, f2 -27, f3 -53; mirrored on the left: anim/variants/dragon_wings.json, `dwing.open`), about 2.2 blocks across at her scale, while the shared flight loops (sec.wings_flap, sec.wings_glide, G10) beat or hold the rig's wing_r and wing_l above them: the two never key the same bone. On the ground a wearer plays its own sec.wings_fold holding wing_r and wing_l near the bind angle (the Ender Dragon's): the shared one turns worn wings in toward the spine, which would cross these folded fans behind the head. `span` scales the wing; `k` also shrinks it with the torso on the smaller forms. The 2D design and the fold were solved offline and written as numbers (notes/artgen.md, \"B5: the Ender Dragon's look\").",
